WEBVTT

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.820
It's chilly.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:14.030
Oh yeah, it's almost Christmas.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:55.670
Well, because it's the Christmas season, I made some special Christmas cakes.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:57.730
That looks delicious!

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:01.110
Chestnuts, and is that white chocolate?

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:01.680
No.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:05.180
Well, you'll know what it is after you taste it.

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:07.020
Let's dig in!

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:12.380
This tastes great.

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:15.730
This chestnut cream is so tasty!

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:19.830
The cassis sauce and the fresh cream go together perfectly.

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:21.760
So it's chestnuts and cassis.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:23.690
Do those really go together that well?

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.040
It's out of this world.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:32.420
The abundant fresh cream brings out the smoothness of the chestnuts and the sweet-and-sour taste of the cassis.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:35.840
Yeah, the fresh cream is essential in this.

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:45.030
This is really good.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.900
Even I would eat this.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:47.800
Isn't it?

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:52.110
The decoration and flavor of Bûche de marron is made for adult tastes.

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:55.050
Then what about this white one, sensei?

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:56.180
Try it.

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:57.140
Okay!

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:02.950
The fresh cream is... The fresh cream is...

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:04.550
Yummy.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:08.340
The cream is like milk turned fluffy.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:10.170
And the strawberries are...

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:12.710
This is based on shortcake.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.500
Shortcake?

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:18.530
You were a pâtissier at a three-star restaurant,

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:22.130
and you're making a Japanese-style cake that's even sold at convenience stores for Christmas?

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:26.650
It's true, shortcake is a Japanese cake,

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:31.390
but there aren't many cakes that are made using just fresh cream and sponge cake.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:32.600
That's marvelous.

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:40.530
Christmas is a good opportunity to show off the great flavor of cakes to those who don't usually eat them.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:47.010
And I think it's a good idea to use shortcake,
because the Japanese are already familiar with it.

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:51.360
Besides, relatively few shops sell really good shortcake.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:53.330
Sorry.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:56.900
That's it! You're quite knowledgeable.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:58.390
Well, not really...

00:03:58.390 --> 00:04:00.780
By the way, officer, how long have you been standing there?

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:04.620
I've retired from the police, and I'm now working privately,

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:05.480
so I'll be going...

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:06.550
Wait a moment...

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:09.970
Thank you very much for your patronage.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:15.070
It's Dome Blanc. If you like it, please try it.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:18.940
We await your next visit.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:23.180
Sensei.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.680
Is a serious man like that your type?

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:26.740
Come to think of it...

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:29.270
he does look a little advanced in years.

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:34.830
Tachibana.

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:38.150
Are these two special Christmas cakes all right with you?

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:39.040
Y-Yeah.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:44.170
Well, so I'm thinking about a delivery service just for Christmas.

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:45.540
Delivery service?

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:48.250
Yes.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:52.390
Free delivery only on December 24th, Christmas Eve.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:54.890
With my Ferrari!

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:56.600
Who'll do this?

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.170
Me, of course.

00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:00.100
And in a Santa costume.

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:04.750
That day, you'll be serving customers by yourself.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:09.770
I can't do something so hard!

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:10.940
Don't cry.
I can't do something so hard!

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:10.980
I can't do something so hard!

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:15.930
Most people would consider an inability to do anything alone after working six months a greater problem.

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:26.910
To be Santa Claus, do I have to shave this stubble?

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:28.260
I don't think so.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:31.350
Santas have beards.

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:32.870
But this is stubble.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:35.860
What?

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:37.250
What's so funny?

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:39.550
No...

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:44.750
It's just that my image of you in high school was of someone cool and aloof.

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:54.330
Well, as I recall, I was in a very tough spot back then.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:55.820
A very tough spot?

00:05:56.690 --> 00:05:58.440
Do you remember Hosoda?

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:00.330
I was going out with her at the time.

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:10.180
O-Okay.

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:14.390
Hey, listen!

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:17.970
After I got back home, I talked with her on the phone for three hours!

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:21.490
We chatted about stuff that wasn't even worth bothering with.

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:22.900
Hey, Tachibana.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:24.740
Why her?

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:26.160
You could've dated someone cuter—

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.320
She's got a huge pair.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:29.110
You breast freak!

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:33.740
I want to break up.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:36.420
Eh?

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:39.360
Wh-Why are you saying this so suddenly, Ayako?

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:42.450
It's not sudden.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:47.760
I decided a while ago

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:50.590
that I'd break up with you when I graduated.

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:52.200
Why?

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:54.150
We're both going to college in Tokyo.

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:55.450
Did I do something wrong?

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:58.980
You're always trying too hard to fit in with me.

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:03.940
You take me where I want to go, you do what I like, you buy what I want.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:06.730
Why are you doing so much for me?

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:09.090
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:11.120
It's because I love you!

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:12.990
I'm happy if you're happy.

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:16.290
You say those things so easily that I can't trust you!

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:19.100
Do you know what the others are saying?

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:22.490
If he's into spectacles, Ono is cuter.

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:26.760
Why is Keiichirou seeing a serious girl like her?

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:30.840
So I switched to contacts and changed my hair.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.000
But now it's...

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:35.880
Who said that?! I'll knock his block off!

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:37.810
I'm seeing someone else.

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:44.560
He's not as good looking or as rich as you,

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:48.410
but when I'm with him, I feel like I'm needed.

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:50.320
I feel like I'm needed.

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:59.100
So that's what happened.

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:03.330
But seriously, am I trying too hard?

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:07.020
After that incident,

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:10.510
it preyed on my mind that other people were worrying about me.

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:13.460
I behaved naturally sometimes,

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:16.510
but I wonder if that made me look like I was trying too hard.

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:21.520
Actually, I wasn't trying too hard, and I just ended up being like this.

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:27.700
Young master!

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:30.380
That scary woman who always comes here is...

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:33.000
Don't cry. Geez.

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:38.710
Welcome, Urushibara-sama.

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:40.410
And thank you for your regular patronage.

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:43.990
Hey, can I reserve a cake that isn't Bûche de marron?

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:45.370
Yes, of course.

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:49.180
We're going to have a party on the 24th,
so I want you to deliver it.

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:50.710
I want Croque en bouche.

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:55.030
Croque en bouche?

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:58.640
You mean the cake that's served at French weddings?

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:01.880
The cake built out of Choux à la Crème?

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:02.810
Yes.

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:06.020
Isn't it beautiful, like a Christmas tree?

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:06.810
If you can't, just say so.

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:12.870
No. We accept your order with pleasure, of course.

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:16.200
Then, I want it decorated with caramel.

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:19.150
Decorated with caramel?

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:25.870
You mean covering the cake with soft caramel threads?

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:27.130
If that's the case,

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:32.510
I suggest that the cake be decorated after delivery rather than before delivery.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:35.170
That would be better, of course.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:36.650
Then I don't have to worry about breakage.

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:39.850
It's more Christmas-like if it's decorated.

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:43.250
If you can't, just say so.

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:45.520
Of course we can.

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:47.000
We accept the order with pleasure.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.480
Then please do that.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:52.480
Caramel decoration?

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:57.540
Umm... Well, I think you can do it, but...

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:58.780
Just as I expected, it requires practice, right?

00:10:00.310 --> 00:10:02.080
Well, in a way...

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:04.130
Yes! It's special training!

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:06.140
You must come to work earlier starting tomorrow, Ono!

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:07.070
Yeah.

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:14.840
Now...

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:17.200
It's only a week until Christmas.

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:19.950
Team pâtissier will work on improving the Christmas cakes.

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:20.540
Yeah.

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:21.380
Gotcha.

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:22.920
I'll be taking special training for decoration.

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:26.310
And Chikage, if you're to serve alone, you'll have to learn how to carry four plates.

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:26.810
Yes.

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:30.780
It's special training. I'm on fire!

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:33.270
Another fan of special training...

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:41.010
You're too tense.

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:42.730
Do it gently.

00:10:42.730 --> 00:10:44.610
L-Like this?

00:10:46.150 --> 00:10:49.810
Now, I assume that many customers will be eating on the premises.

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:51.430
First, how to carry four plates at once.

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:53.630
You carry three like this.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:55.560
Here and here and here.

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:56.430
Now, you try it!

00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:57.840
Y-Yes.

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:01.300
I-Is it like this?

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:04.090
Oh, you can do it.

00:11:04.090 --> 00:11:06.250
Your hands are so large that it must be easy.

00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:08.350
Young master.

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:09.070
What?

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:12.350
I-I don't know which plate to put down first!

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:16.480
I wonder if there's a major league garçon training harness?

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:19.720
So should we get started?

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:20.320
Yes!

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:22.010
Kanda-kun.

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:25.720
Try making it all by yourself, from the cream to the decoration.

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:26.490
Eh?

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:28.670
It's a good time to step up.

00:11:29.310 --> 00:11:31.100
I'll just watch and say nothing.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:31.880
Yes!

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:43.070
Sorry!

00:11:43.070 --> 00:11:45.090
The cream is messed up again!

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:48.780
You don't have to apologize. Just think why it turned out like this.

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:49.530
Yes.

00:11:49.530 --> 00:11:50.800
Hey, Ono.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:53.220
I want more special training on decoration.

00:11:53.220 --> 00:11:54.860
So I won't sleep tonight again.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:04.120
All right!

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:07.440
We have quite a lot of orders, and it's time to get started.

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:09.890
Do it with care, you guys.

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:11.240
Yes.

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:14.360
What, what. Where's your spirit?

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:18.830
That's because I had to give you special training for caramel decoration.

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:21.720
How's this?

00:12:22.190 --> 00:12:24.370
Well, a rather poorly built Santa.

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:26.340
Quite a poorly built Santa...

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:27.440
What?

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:28.850
You look good, young master!

00:12:29.630 --> 00:12:30.650
All right!

00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:31.980
Well, I'm going to make my rounds!

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:37.140
Young master, have a safe trip!

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:40.900
Well, he's trying too hard. He really doesn't fit in that.

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:43.860
If Tachibana wants to do it...

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:52.180
Merry Christmas!

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:59.830
Oh my! Are you scared?

00:12:59.830 --> 00:13:05.570
I'm sorry, since you took the trouble to come here dressed like Santa.

00:13:05.570 --> 00:13:06.850
N-No.

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:08.100
I'm sorry for making your baby cry.

00:13:09.210 --> 00:13:12.620
He's crying as if the bogeyman had come!

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:17.360
Merry Christmas!

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:21.980
Can't you go along with his pretense?

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:24.340
He's doing it because it's his job.

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:26.820
I'm heart-broken.

00:13:27.100 --> 00:13:29.780
Oh, you don't look good in that.

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:33.050
I feel sorry for handsome men in this situation.

00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:35.550
Santa should be chubby.

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:42.420
Okay!

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:45.880
This is really good.

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:48.940
You're getting better, Kanda-kun.

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:50.130
Are you sure?!

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:52.190
You're making wonderful progress.

00:13:52.190 --> 00:13:53.370
Thank you very much!

00:13:54.360 --> 00:13:58.640
Oh, yeah, I wonder if gramps' Croque en bouche went well.

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:01.350
I don't know.

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:23.130
If this doesn't work well at the next place, I'll take the costume off.

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:26.840
That house at last, huh?

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:33.350
Is this possible? I'm glad Santa Claus came on Christmas Eve!

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:36.680
Everyone look, it's Santa-san!

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:43.820
So after all, drunk grown-ups are the only ones who are delighted.

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:47.990
Merry Christmas!

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:49.240
But I'm very happy!

00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:51.280
This is Croque en bouche.

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:53.810
It's looks nice.

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:56.280
Wonderful. Those are Choux à la Crème, right?

00:14:56.280 --> 00:14:57.250
Indeed they are.

00:14:57.250 --> 00:14:59.080
Oh. This isn't all, is it?

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:02.170
The real thing starts now, right?

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:03.400
Santa-san.

00:15:04.650 --> 00:15:07.580
Would you let me use the kitchen for a while?

00:15:14.380 --> 00:15:16.010
What are you doing?

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:18.970
I'm softening caramel and sugar.

00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:20.350
Well, I think it's all right.

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:25.010
God, Buddha,

00:15:25.010 --> 00:15:27.620
gifted pâtissier Ono-sama.

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:30.070
Please let me succeed!

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:44.150
You're great, Santa-san.

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:47.090
I'm already a fan of this Santa-san.

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:49.510
Come on, Papa. You've drunk too much.

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:54.200
We have to go to granny's place in Nakano to pick up Akira.

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:55.130
Eh?

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:56.470
But Mama!

00:15:57.050 --> 00:15:57.690
S-So these two are husband and wife.

00:15:57.690 --> 00:16:01.940
I'll miss you Santa-san, but bye-bye.

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:06.310
Chikage-san.

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:07.940
How is it going?

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:10.600
We sold out just now.

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:11.770
Really?

00:16:13.690 --> 00:16:15.210
Yeah!

00:16:15.210 --> 00:16:17.650
The deliveries are done, and I'm back.

00:16:18.900 --> 00:16:21.100
Hey, where are the customers? What the...

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:23.790
Look in the showcase, Tachibana.

00:16:27.110 --> 00:16:28.460
We did it!

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:31.840
Hey, Chikage. You were useful today, right?

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:32.880
No, not in the least.

00:16:33.290 --> 00:16:36.240
I let Kanda-san handle most of the takeout.

00:16:36.240 --> 00:16:37.430
You're too honest.

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:39.680
How did your deliveries go?

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:42.890
Huh! It was like one win and twenty-nine losses.

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:47.990
Well, kids aren't expecting a well-groomed Santa.

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:51.920
So I must've been trying too hard.

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:06.420
Gramps.

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:08.930
What?

00:17:08.930 --> 00:17:11.610
I think your Santa was a good idea.

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:12.090
Huh?

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:14.860
A customer phoned to say,

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:17.040
"I couldn't tell you when you came,

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:19.580
but my daughter was very happy.

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:21.520
Thank you so much."

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:25.530
Really?

00:17:25.530 --> 00:17:26.440
Yeah!

00:17:29.760 --> 00:17:31.080
Hey, Eiji.

00:17:31.080 --> 00:17:31.750
Huh?

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:34.820
When I was abducted,

00:17:35.250 --> 00:17:38.840
the kidnapper didn't demand any money, not even once.

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:47.380
He may have intended to molest me.

00:17:47.380 --> 00:17:51.090
Maybe that's why I can't remember what happened then.

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:54.560
The fact that the people around me were worried

00:17:54.560 --> 00:17:56.880
preyed on my mind.

00:17:56.880 --> 00:18:00.750
And before I realized it, I was the one worrying about the people around me.

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:07.480
Happy birthday!

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:09.340
There you go.

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:10.760
Everyone, please eat a lot.

00:18:10.760 --> 00:18:12.800
Ma'am, this is really nice.

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:13.820
Oh! Thank you.

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:18.280
Keiichirou.

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:19.560
What about some more cake?

00:18:19.560 --> 00:18:21.620
Umm, yeah. I need the bathroom.

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:22.580
I see.

00:18:29.530 --> 00:18:32.420
I'm glad your son is all right now.

00:18:33.020 --> 00:18:34.480
I don't think so.

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:40.530
It's only been a month, and already he said that he wanted to have a birthday party.

00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:43.370
He's just as he used to be.

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:45.740
He told a funny story today.

00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:47.100
He's too cheerful.

00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:49.540
Madame.

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:54.820
He still can't remember anything about the incident.

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:57.120
I wonder what awful memories he had.

00:18:57.120 --> 00:18:58.370
Madame.

00:18:58.370 --> 00:19:02.930
He has a long life ahead of him, many years,

00:19:02.930 --> 00:19:06.370
and he'll have to deal with the scar in his mind.

00:19:06.800 --> 00:19:08.740
What did my son ever do...

00:19:08.740 --> 00:19:11.790
I will never forgive the kidnapper.

00:19:23.110 --> 00:19:25.990
So that's why I'm like this, even at my age.

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:28.580
Hey, I think it's all right to try too hard.

00:19:29.750 --> 00:19:36.190
For me, being unruly felt better than receiving solicitous care as a "poor orphan."

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:39.950
I think you should do whatever you want.

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:48.900
Why do I have to be cheered up by a kid?!

00:19:48.900 --> 00:19:50.610
Shut up! You ruined my efforts—

00:19:50.610 --> 00:19:51.390
Tachibana.

00:19:52.350 --> 00:19:56.010
I made some side dishes that I'd like to sell with the sweets.

00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:57.310
Would you try them?

00:19:57.310 --> 00:19:58.340
Side dishes?

00:19:58.340 --> 00:19:59.340
Yes, traiteur.

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:01.260
Traiteur?

00:20:07.770 --> 00:20:12.730
French cake shops usually sell side dishes and breads.

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:16.060
I want to sell them too, starting next year.

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:19.170
Well, only if you say it's all right, of course.

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:20.990
Let me see.

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:26.260
Terrific!

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:28.600
This terrine of spear squid and lobster.

00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:30.170
Aspic of smoked salmon.

00:20:30.170 --> 00:20:31.620
Goat cheese pizza.

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:33.210
Bacon quiche.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:35.330
These make me want a glass of wine.

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:36.420
Here you go, young master.

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:39.370
Aren't you considerate today?

00:20:39.370 --> 00:20:39.630
Yes.

00:20:42.940 --> 00:20:46.090
I want to make this shop a place

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:51.110
where someone who is always trying too hard can get relief

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:52.740
by eating my sweets and side dishes.

00:20:55.390 --> 00:20:56.610
Merry Christmas.

00:20:58.430 --> 00:21:00.080
Merry Christmas!

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:05.290
This is sparkling juice for kids.

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:06.920
Of course.

00:21:06.920 --> 00:21:09.010
We have to get up early tomorrow.

00:21:10.230 --> 00:21:12.630
Let me have a drink!
